<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix19: OgreStack silently refuses to stack AV_CompressedWaste, and no Overrides.xml entry can
       make it work.

       [AV] Mechtech (3339795890) defines the item in 1.6/Defs/Items_WasteContainment.xml with a
       single category, and its own comment shows the author was unhappy with the choice:
           <thingCategories>
             <!-\- <li>ItemsMisc</li>  until I find out how to remove it from shelfs-\->
             <li>Chunks</li>
           </thingCategories>

       OgreStack (1447140290) bans a fixed set of categories outright. Decompiled 2026-08-14 from
       1.6/Assemblies/OgreStack.dll:

           private static readonly HashSet<string> _CATEGORIES_BANNED =
               { "Chunks", "Furniture", "StoneChunks", "WeaponsMelee", "Books" };

           // ModifyStackSizes(), per ThingDef:
           int itemLevelOverride = individualOverrides.GetItemLevelOverride(allDef.defName);
           if (itemLevelOverride > 0) { allDef.stackLimit = itemLevelOverride; }   // user value applied
           if (individualOverrides.IsCategoryBanned(allDef.FirstThingCategory.ToString()))
           { allDef.stackLimit = 1; }                                              // then clobbered

       The two ifs are sequential with no else, so a banned category ALWAYS beats a user override.
       The Overrides.xml entry is read and applied, then reset to 1 one line later - which is why the
       entry still shows in OgreStack's settings window (DoSettingsWindowContents renders the parsed
       file via ViewInternalOverrides) while the live stackLimit stays at 1. Menu and behaviour read
       from different places.

       Patching <stackLimit> directly does NOT work: OgreStack rewrites stackLimit on every ThingDef
       at startup, after all XML patches have run. The only thing that helps is changing what
       OgreStack SEES, so FirstThingCategory is no longer a banned one.

       Replace Chunks with ItemsMisc - the category the author originally wanted. OgreStack then
       applies the Overrides.xml value normally.

       SIDE EFFECT (accepted deliberately): thingCategories drives storage/bill filter placement, so
       compressed waste now appears under Items > Misc rather than Chunks. Stockpile and shelf
       filters that were set to accept Chunks will no longer include it, and any existing zone
       configured that way needs re-ticking. The author's comment suggests shelf behaviour was the
       reason for Chunks in the first place, so watch for compressed waste becoming shelf-storable.

       Requires a matching entry in OgreStack's Overrides.xml, which is user config and lives outside
       this repo:
           <item defName="AV_CompressedWaste" stackLimit="100" />

       success is NOT Always - if [AV] Mechtech restructures this def we want to be told rather than
       have the fix rot silently, as Fix14 did. PatchOperationFindMod already makes it inert when the
       mod is absent. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>[AV] Mechtech</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AV_CompressedWaste"]/thingCategories</xpath>
      <value>
        <thingCategories>
          <li>ItemsMisc</li>
        </thingCategories>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
